# Run build after changes

After making **any code changes** in this repo (not for read-only questions or reviews), run the build before finishing the task.

## Required command

From the repo root:

```bash
npm run build:check
```

This runs TypeScript checking and the Vite production build.

## When to run

- After editing, adding, or deleting source files
- Before telling the user the task is complete
- If the build fails, fix the errors and re-run until it passes

## When to skip

- User asked a question only (no file edits)
- Read-only exploration or code review with no modifications
- Build already passed in the same turn after the latest edits

## If you also changed the backend

When edits span repos, also run validation in `../ei-website-backend`:

```bash
cd ../ei-website-backend && npm run test:math
```

Report build/test failures clearly; do not leave broken builds for the user to discover.
